    "result": "The tests aren't in the workspace, so I couldn't run any. The fix is a one-line change in `sqlparse/engine/statement_splitter.py`.\n\nIn `_handle_closing_keyword`, the `END` branch had an inverted condition. It called `self._block_stack.pop()` when the stack was empty, which raises `IndexError: pop from empty list`. I changed `if not (self._block_stack):` to `if self._block_stack:`, so it only pops when there is something to pop. That is the error your first failing check reports, and it fires on any statement with a `CASE ... END`, so it plausibly accounts for the other 21 too."
  },
